PSthreads and UthLib
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Description:
UthLib (Underlying Threads Library) is a portable non-preemptive
thread package for building two-level thread libraries on top of
POSIX Threads.

PSthreads (Process Scope threads) is a runtime library that
takes advantage of UthLib and implements and two-level thread
model.

License: 
Since UthLib has been derived from the State Threads Library,
it is distributed according to the Mozilla Public License Version


For more information: 
Read the included documentation file.




-----------------------------------------------------------------------

./configure \
    CC="clang -std=gnu17" \
    CPPFLAGS="-D_XOPEN_SOURCE=700 -D_DARWIN_C_SOURCE" \
    CFLAGS="-O2 -Wno-deprecated-declarations" \
    --with-csm=mcsc \
    --with-sync=mutex \
    --with-maxvps=64 \
    --enable-stealing
